        "caption": "Congratulations to Rutgers alums Tom Pelphrey and Katie Dippold, who both won Emmy Awards on Monday evening at the Peacock Theater in Los Angeles.\n\nPelphrey (MGSA \u201904) won for Outstanding Supporting Actor in a Drama Series. He received the accolade for his performance as Robbie Prendergast in the HBO crime drama series Task.\n\nDippold (SC&I \u201902) won for Outstanding Writing for a Comedy Series for the Apple TV+ horror-comedy series Widow's Bay. She also accepted the Emmy for Outstanding Comedy Series as the creator, writer, and executive producer of the show, which set a single-season comedy record with 14 wins.\n\nPelphrey joins James Gandolfini and Sheryl Lee Ralph among alums who have won Primetime Emmys in the acting category, while Dippold joins Mike Sweeney and Christopher Markus in the writing category. #rutgerspride\n\n\ud83d\udcf8: Phil McCarten/Invision for the Television Academy/AP Content Services",
